--- a/.andromeda/security-plan.md
+++ b/.andromeda/security-plan.md
@@ -11,3 +11,3 @@
 decision/child-output-tolerant-unknown · Child output parsing fails to unknown — Child output parsing is tolerant, and a failure becomes unknown or a closed failure word.
-decision/child-path-trust · Child processes trust PATH — Spawned child processes are whatever the calling process's PATH resolves to.
+decision/child-path-trust · Child processes trust PATH — Spawned child processes are whatever the calling process's PATH resolves to. · except: viola console's action children are viola's own executable, never a PATH lookup. · provisional
 decision/ci-no-secrets-no-real-claude · CI holds no secrets — CI holds no secrets and never runs the real claude CLI, which runs only locally.
@@ -233,3 +233,6 @@
 decision/config-tolerant-parse · Tolerant config parse — config.json is parsed tolerantly, unknown keys counted, its v checked and its read capped at MAX_FRAME; a bad value falls back to its default and is reported as parse-rejected.
-decision/console-key-reader-bounded · Console key reader bounded and closed — viola console reads the human's keys from its own terminal in raw mode in reads of at most 64 bytes, each read decoded to one closed class: 0x03 anywhere is interrupt, exactly q is quit, anything else is unbound; no key byte reaches any log line or output. · guard: console_logs_an_unbound_key_by_class_alone · provisional
+decision/console-editing-line-bounded · Console editing line bounded — The console's editing line holds at most MAX_FRAME bytes, a char past the bound counted unbound and appended to nothing; Enter, Escape and Interrupt end the read and the rest of that read is dropped. · provisional
+decision/console-key-reader-bounded · Console key reader bounded and closed — viola console reads the human's keys from its own terminal in raw mode in reads of at most 64 bytes, each read decoded into keys of closed classes, an escape sequence bounded in its wait and its length; no key byte reaches any log line. · guard: console_logs_an_unbound_key_by_class_alone · provisional
+decision/console-runs-verbs-as-children · Console runs its actions as children of its own exe — viola console runs every action as a child of its own executable with --home, the verb and the name, VIOLA_NAME and VIOLA_DIR removed, never through a shell and one child at a time; each output stream is read under MAX_FRAME and each line escaped before it is drawn.
+decision/console-typed-text-as-data · Console hands typed text to its verbs as data only — viola console hands typed text to its verbs as data only: send's text on stdin unchanged, switch's words only as --effort= or --model= values never as flags, open's typed name as one argv element, and answer's body a closed behaviour word on stdin. · provisional
 decision/dialog-free-text-character-set · Dialog free text uses the paste text set — Dialog free text (permission and plan messages, question answer values) is held to the same exact character set as paste text.
@@ -376,3 +379,6 @@
 decision/code-bearing-files-rewritten-each-start · Code-bearing files rewritten at every start — The plugin files are rewritten whole at every start, a revived start included, with mode 0600 set before the write, never reusing an existing copy. · why: A code-bearing file written at every start and handed to the CLI is a ratified boundary widening.
+decision/console-action-child-outlives-quit · Console action child may outlive a quit — A console action child may outlive the console's quit; no parent-death tie is set.
 decision/console-agents-child-outlives-quit · Console agents child may outlive a quit — A claude agents child of viola console may outlive a quit of the console by up to its 5 s bound. · why: Accepted as built. · provisional
+decision/console-answer-reads-kind-and-id · Console answer prompt reads the dialog kind and id only — The console's answer prompt reads only the board's pending dialog kind and id, never dialog, question or option text; a pending question draws one fixed line and starts no child.
+decision/console-diagnostics-closed-words · Console diagnostics lines hold closed words and counts — The console-action diagnostics line holds the verb word and exit code only, and a console-key line a closed key word and a key count only; no name, argument, typed text or child output reaches any line. · provisional
 decision/cross-session-fixture-keeps-runtime-path · Cross-session fixture keeps the sender's socket address — The committed cross-session fixture keeps, inside the CLI's own prefix, the recording host's runtime-dir path and pids; the record scrub does not normalise them. · why: An accepted residual.
